  item(200,'P000319','theorem','The uniform relative-commutant criterion for a factor state',r'The displayed theorem says \(\forall x\,\forall\varepsilon>0\,\exists y\) satisfying the correlation estimate, with \(y\) in a local commutant.',r'For a state \(\varphi\) of the spin UHF algebra, \(M_\varphi\) is a factor if and only if for every \(x\in\mathcal A\) and \(\varepsilon>0\) there exists \(n\) such that \[|\varphi(xy)-\varphi(x)\varphi(y)|\leq\varepsilon\|y\|\quad\text{for all }y\in\mathcal A([-n,n])^{\prime}\cap\mathcal A.\] The quantifier is over every element of the tail relative commutant, not one chosen \(y\).',r'\citet[Theorem~2.5 and proof; Russian translation pp.~100--101]{powers1967representations} gives this criterion, after rescaling \(x\) to incorporate \(\varepsilon\). The original theorem is 1967; the Russian translation available to the seminar is 1969.',refs=['powers1967representations'],literal='false as written',development='annotated',problem='GP-1970-22',status='Established with the corrected uniform quantifiers. The literal existential condition is vacuous because \(y=0\) always works.')
