  item(201,'P000323','construction','Residue pairing with the restricted linear dual',r'\(H^{n-1}=\operatorname{Hom}_{R}(R,k)\) is written twice, with \(k\) the evaluation-at-zero module; the proposed pairing takes the coefficient of \((x_1\cdots x_n)^{-1}\).',r'Over a field \(k\), the pairing \(\langle f,\eta\rangle=\operatorname{coeff}_{x_1^{-1}\cdots x_n^{-1}}(f\eta)\) is nondegenerate and identifies top cohomology with the finite-support, or graded restricted, \(k\)-linear dual \(R^\circ=\bigoplus_{d\geq0}\operatorname{Hom}_k(R_d,k)\), with the grading shifted by \(-n\). Its \(R\)-action is \((r\ell)(f)=\ell(rf)\). It is neither \(\operatorname{Hom}_R(R,k)\cong k\) nor the full algebraic dual \(\prod_d\operatorname{Hom}_k(R_d,k)\).',r'The monomial bases in \citet[Lemma~30.8.1]{stacks2026projective} verify the pairing term by term. The source\'s reference to Serre duality is a thematic link: this affine local-duality calculation needs the restricted dual and the differential/degree convention stated here.',refs=['stacks2026projective','serre1955coherent'],literal='false as written',match='partial',development='annotated',problem='GP-1970-25',status='The corrected residue-dual identification is established. The displayed \(R\)-linear Hom has the wrong dimension and action.')
